From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:32:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: do not take a swap_pace floor above
 600 us

swap_pace starts a held swap the lead before the tick ahead of the one
it aims at, plus swap_pace_margin_us (520 us). A lead more than that
margin above the firmware's real floor therefore starts the swap early
enough to make the tick before the aim, and a lead well below the floor
starts it too late for the aim; any lead within about 0.5 ms above or
1 ms below the floor lands on the aim.

The floor is learned as the shortest start-to-completion time of a
window of 64 unheld swaps outside video. It measured 0.19 to 0.35 ms on
every boot, but on 1.728, during one fullscreen 1080p60 YouTube run,
it rose from 0.19 to 1.72 ms although swaps started less than two ticks
after a completion are no longer learned from: a window of swaps that
all start at about the same distance before a tick, as when a
compositor answers each completion after the same render time, holds
nothing shorter than that distance.

Do not take a learned value above 600 us; keep the last one.
swap_pace_lead_us still sets any lead by hand.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index c989837d99..f3943ef5e5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -1792,11 +1792,22 @@ static bool dcp_m4_int_late_d590(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r, u32 id)
  * also grow.
  */
 #define DCP_M4_PACE_WINDOW	64
+/*
+ * The longest floor taken. A lead more than swap_pace_margin_us above the
+ * real floor starts a held swap early enough to make the tick before the
+ * one aimed at, and the floor measured 0.19 to 0.35 ms on every boot. Yet
+ * windows of swaps that all started at about the same distance before a
+ * tick (as when a compositor answers each completion after the same render
+ * time) held nothing shorter, and raised the estimate to 1.6 to 1.7 ms
+ * during fullscreen video, swaps started two ticks or more after a
+ * completion included (measured). Such a window is not taken.
+ */
+#define DCP_M4_PACE_LEAD_MAX_US	600
 
 static void dcp_m4_pace_learn(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r)
 {
 	u64 start = READ_ONCE(r->int_start_cnt), done = READ_ONCE(r->int_done_cnt), lat;
-	u64 e = READ_ONCE(r->pace_e), prev = r->int_prev_done;
+	u64 e = READ_ONCE(r->pace_e), prev = r->int_prev_done, max;
 
 	if (r->int_prev_done && done > r->int_prev_done) {
 		/*
@@ -1854,12 +1865,14 @@ static void dcp_m4_pace_learn(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r)
 	if (prev && start < prev + div_u64(arch_timer_get_cntfrq(), 120))
 		return;
 	lat = done - start;
+	max = div_u64(arch_timer_get_cntfrq() * DCP_M4_PACE_LEAD_MAX_US, USEC_PER_SEC);
 	if (!r->int_lat_n || lat < r->int_lat_win)
 		r->int_lat_win = lat;
-	if (!READ_ONCE(r->int_lat_min) || lat < READ_ONCE(r->int_lat_min))
+	if (lat <= max && (!READ_ONCE(r->int_lat_min) || lat < READ_ONCE(r->int_lat_min)))
 		WRITE_ONCE(r->int_lat_min, lat);
 	if (++r->int_lat_n >= DCP_M4_PACE_WINDOW) {
-		WRITE_ONCE(r->int_lat_min, r->int_lat_win);
+		if (r->int_lat_win <= max)
+			WRITE_ONCE(r->int_lat_min, r->int_lat_win);
 		r->int_lat_n = 0;
 	}
 }
